Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Bearing Drift
- Story & Context: When the navigation computer miscalculated and locked the crew in a sector of absolute darkness, Jax used a sharpened soldering iron to carve the coordinates into the bulkhead. The sound of the metal scraping against metal mimicked the rhythm of the life-support fans, creating an accidental percussion loop that never stopped. "Where the needle stops, the gravity bleeds," Jax muttered while the air pressure alarm shrieked a high-pitched F-sharp in the background. 
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A solitary, rusted compass needle spinning frantically against a backdrop of deep indigo cosmic dust and cold, sharp white stars; photorealistic texture of weathered titanium.

Track 2: Port-Side Orison
- Story & Context: Kael sits by the viewing port every cycle, whispering prayers to a planet he knows he will never step foot on, holding a vial of recycled condensation he calls his "sea." His confession is a quiet one, a heavy sigh against the DX7’s shivering digital bell patches that sound like ice forming on the inside of the glass. He admits to stealing the last of the ship's fuel cells to keep the internal heaters running for the synth, whispering "there is no harbor, only the hunger." 
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A blurry, tear-streaked face reflected in a thick, reinforced porthole glass, with the faint glow of an impossibly distant, alien sun bleeding through the frame.

Track 3: The Keel Stays Silent
- Story & Context: Years after the migration ended, the ship drifted into a gravity well, and the legend of the "Silent Keel" became the only religion left to the children born in the hulls. Every anniversary, the survivors gather to play this hymn, a booming, distorted anthem that sounds like the hull finally splitting under the pressure of the truth. As the feedback swell reaches its peak, the final line "the rust remembers what the engine forgot" echoes through the empty mess hall, marking the final departure from the home they never had. 
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A massive, jagged skeletal structure of a derelict spaceship floating in a nebula, shaped vaguely like an ancient maritime galleon; surreal, dark, ethereal, grand scale.

